---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import Prose from '../../components/Prose.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  locale="en"
  title="About — Luvita"
  description="Luvita is an independent software product company, founder-led, with an engineering practice formed in banking and enterprise systems."
  paths={{ tr: 'hakkimizda', en: 'about' }}
>
  <Hero
    eyebrow="About"
    title="We answer to our own roadmap."
    lead="We build software products of our own, with working habits formed in banking and enterprise systems."
  />

  <section class="container">
    <Prose>
      <p>
        Luvita is an independent software company: we build, ship and maintain
        products of our own. Most of our background is in banking and
        enterprise systems, and our working habits were formed there.
      </p>
      <p>
        Luvita is founder-led — every product is engineered end to end by the
        same hands, from the first commit to the maintenance years later. Our founder has more than a
        decade of experience in banking and finance: at Türk Eximbank, at
        Channel Capital Advisors in London, and most recently at ING. Our core competencies are
        Java/Spring Boot backend systems, cross-platform applications with
        Flutter, and cloud architectures.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our apps ship under the <strong>CosmoCrew</strong> brand: SliceFocus,
        LexiPower and With Handlebars are all live and actively maintained.
        Our focus going forward is growing products of our own, starting
        with <strong>Umay</strong> and <strong>Pelerin</strong>.
      </p>
      <h2>How we work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Significant architecture decisions are written down, so the
          reasoning behind them can be traced years later.
        </li>
        <li>
          Testing and automation are set up on day one, not bolted on at the
          end.
        </li>
        <li>
          Once a product is live, it stays under our care — every app we have
          shipped is proof of that.
        </li>
        <li>
          We say where a product stands, what is missing and what it will
          take — as it is.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </Prose>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
